+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know relative clauses with *que* and *quien* from B1 Unit 5. A relative clause adds information about a noun without starting a new sentence: *la planta que crece en el agua*. *Que* works for things, animals and people. *Quien* is only for people, and it is most useful after a preposition: *la guía con quien viajamos*. Here you use them to describe the high plateau and Lake Titicaca."
