+      "title": "What you already know",
+      "content": "You know *antes de que* and *después de que* from B2 Unit 7. *Antes de que* always takes the subjunctive: after a past verb, the imperfect subjunctive (*antes de que llegaran*). *Después de que* takes the indicative for something that happened (*después de que llegaron*) and the subjunctive for something still to come. The two are ideal for putting the events of a single day in order."
